      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A legally sound written warning must include a clear description of the unsatisfactory performance, specific dates and times of incidents during the previous period, and explicit examples of the expected coaching provided before this step. It should also outline a measurable corrective action plan with strict deadlines and a signature acknowledging receipt from the employee. If they repeat the same small mistakes, you must formally escalate this specific behavior in subsequent documents to demonstrate a proven pattern of non-compliance rather than isolated incidents.",
